WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.330
In 2022, Rantanen and colleagues checked
several observational datasets for the

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.130
Arctic, from 1979 to 2021.

3
00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:13.350
They found it had warmed nearly
4 times faster than the globe.

4
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.730
Earlier studies had
reported two to three times.

5
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.930
Climate models rarely
reproduce a ratio that high.

6
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.330
So why there?

7
00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.850
Is the Arctic closer to the Sun in summer?

8
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.250
Has it lost its ozone layer?

9
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:30.530
In this mission, you'll see how feedback
loops can amplify or dampen a change

10
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:31.770
in climate.

11
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:36.510
Then you'll weigh how big, and how soon,
the carbon in thawing permafrost and

12
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.730
wetland methane could matter.

13
00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:43.590
Your mission: explain why the Arctic has
warmed nearly four times as fast as the

14
00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:44.280
planet.
